The key insight: since there is only one producer and one consumer, we can use simple atomic counters (head and tail indices) to coordinate access without CAS loops or mutexes.

---

## Data Structure

```
+------------------------------------------+
|           Ring Buffer (size N)            |
|  [0] [1] [2] ... [N-2] [N-1]            |
+------------------------------------------+

Producer maintains: write_index (how many items written)
Consumer maintains: read_index  (how many items read)

The buffer is full when: (write_index - read_index) == N
The buffer is empty when: write_index == read_index
```

We use **monotonically increasing indices** rather than wrapping indices modulo N for the atomic counters. This avoids ambiguity in comparing positions. The actual array index is computed as `index % N`.

